.TH COURIER 1 "November 2026" "Courier 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
courier \- local Gmail client for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B courier
.RB [ \-\-serve ]
.RB [ \-\-data-dir
.IR DIRECTORY ]
.RB [ \-\-minimized ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Courier
is a desktop Gmail client built with Python, GTK 3, and WebKitGTK.
It merges multiple Gmail accounts into one inbox and keeps mail data
in a local SQLite database.
.PP
The first launch asks for a Google Desktop OAuth client in Settings.
Mail is fetched from Gmail; the local HTTP server listens only on
127.0.0.1.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-serve
Run only the local HTTP server, without opening a GTK window.
.TP
.BI \-\-data-dir " DIRECTORY"
Use a different runtime data directory instead of
.IR ~/.local/share/courier .
.TP
.B \-\-minimized
Start with only the tray icon visible.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show the command-line help and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B COURIER_DATA_DIR
Overrides the runtime data directory.
.TP
.B COURIER_DEV=1
Enables the WebKit inspector and console output.
.TP
.B COURIER_DEMO=1
Skips Gmail sync. Intended for the sample database.
.TP
.B COURIER_GPU=1
Leaves WebKit hardware acceleration enabled.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/courier/courier.db
SQLite database containing account metadata, OAuth tokens, cached
mail, drafts, and settings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/courier/courier.log
Sync and provider errors. Tokens are not written to the log.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/courier.desktop
Optional login entry created by Settings.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project home page:
.UR https://github.com/joelis10/courier
.UE
